    {
      "statement": "The patient is an 85-year-old male with a history of prostate adenocarcinoma (initially localized, Gleason 7) who has experienced intermittent disease progression and recurrence between ages 77.7 and 82.2, followed by a period of stable disease with undetectable PSA (0.0 ng/ml) and no radiographic progression from age 82.6 to 85.0. The most recent clinical assessment at age 85.0 explicitly states there is no evidence of cancer recurrence or progression within the past 24 months.",
      "relation": "NEI",
      "citations": [
        {
