    },
    {
      "statement": "The patient's genomic profile includes somatic mutations in SPOP and ZFHX3, and copy number alterations in PMAIP1, CDKN1B, APC, BCL2, and ETV6. SPOP mutations are associated with favorable prognosis in localized prostate cancer, while CDKN1B loss and ZFHX3 mutations can be associated with more aggressive disease or progression. However, the clinical trajectory over the last 2.5 years (ages 82.6-85.0) has been stable with no progression despite these molecular features.",
      "relation": "NEI",
      "citations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "file-db0399a80c37cc33b78c:f02"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "file-ac19fb1315da39246b4d:f01"
        }
      ],
      "used_claim_ids": [
        "literature-02"
      ],
      "scope": "relationship",
      "evidence_level": "measured",
      "material_status": "present"
    },
    {
      "statement": "The patient's performance status declined from ECOG 0 to ECOG 3 between ages 84.6 and 85.0, indicating significant functional impairment. While the cancer itself has not progressed radiographically or biochemically in the last 24 months, the severe decline in performance status at age 85 introduces uncertainty regarding the patient's ability to tolerate future treatments if progression were to occur, and may confound the interpretation of 'progression' in terms of clinical outcome.",
